From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 05:06:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The About tab takes the secret replacements whole: no race
 with a mod load

The asset replacer rebuilt its secret replacements (updateSecretReplacements) on DXVK's command
thread when mods finished loading, changed or reloaded, while the About tab
(ImGuiAbout::Secrets::update) walked the same map on the game's present thread every frame, with a
plain bool between them. GMod died with a null read in Secrets::update a few seconds after Remix
loaded its mods (the field, 2026-11-15). The command thread now builds the map on its own, checks the
selected variants against it, and publishes it whole under a lock (SecretHandoff,
rtx_secret_handoff.h); the About tab takes a copy under the same lock. A load without secret
replacements leaves the tab's copy as it was, as before.

rtx_secret_handoff.h is self-contained; tests/rtx/unit/test_secret_handoff.cpp covers it (a publish
taken once, a load without secrets, the newest publish wins, a copy outlives the next publish, the
command and present threads).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
